{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2128-06-09 13:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee. I'll be taking care of you during your stay. You're here for a scheduled ERCP today, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2128-06-09 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that's right. I had a stent placed before, and they said I needed to come back to get it removed and checked."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2128-06-09 13:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s correct. But during the procedure today, we found some new issues. There’s a narrowing — we call it a stricture — in your pancreatic duct, and there are still several stones."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2128-06-09 13:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh no. So they couldn’t just remove the old stent?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2128-06-09 13:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did remove the old stent, but because of the blockage and stones, we had to place a new one to keep the duct open. We also widened the narrowed area with a small balloon and removed a few stones."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2128-06-09 13:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been having a lot of pain in my upper belly, going to my back. Is that from this?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2128-06-09 13:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s very likely related. The stones and narrowing can cause pressure and inflammation in the pancreas, which leads to that kind of pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2128-06-09 13:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And what about my blood sugar? I’ve been passing out — had a few low sugar episodes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2128-06-09 13:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your blood sugar was low when you arrived — 52. You mentioned you already reduced your insulin. We’ve kept it at 8 units in the morning and 4 at night to avoid more lows."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2128-06-09 13:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. That’s been helping. I was scared I’d end up in a coma again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2128-06-09 13:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re monitoring it closely. Your sugars have been between 100 and 250 since then, which is much safer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2128-06-09 13:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. What happens now? Do I stay long?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2128-06-09 13:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll stay for a couple of days. We want to make sure you can eat without nausea, your pain is manageable, and your labs stay stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2128-06-09 13:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been nauseous. Is that normal after the procedure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2128-06-09 13:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s common. We’ll give you something for that. You’ll stay on IV fluids for now and start small sips tomorrow if you’re stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2128-06-09 13:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my pain — it’s still pretty bad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2128-06-09 13:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know. We’re giving you IV pain medication. It should help. The pain may take a few days to settle as the inflammation goes down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2128-06-09 13:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had this for years. It’s just worse lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2128-06-09 13:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your chronic pancreatitis makes this more complex. We’re managing it step by step. The stent should help reduce pressure and prevent more damage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2128-06-10 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2128-06-10 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little better. I had some juice this morning and didn’t throw up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2128-06-10 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great progress. We’ll keep advancing your diet — maybe soft foods today if you tolerate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2128-06-10 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my blood sugar?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2128-06-10 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Still stable. 122 this morning. We’ll keep the same insulin dose for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2128-06-10 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. When can I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2128-06-10 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly tomorrow, if you keep improving. You need to be pain-controlled, eating, and stable on your insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2128-06-10 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And what about the stent? Do I have to come back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2128-06-10 09:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll need another ERCP in about eight weeks to remove the stent and check if the duct is healing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2128-06-10 09:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need more stents?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2128-06-10 09:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll see then. The goal is that with the dilation and stent, the duct stays open. But we’ll reassess at that time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2128-06-10 09:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’m just tired of being sick."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2128-06-10 09:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. We’re doing everything we can to reduce flare-ups. Staying off alcohol is also very important to prevent further damage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2128-06-10 09:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know. I’ve been trying. It’s hard with everything else going on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2128-06-10 09:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We can connect you with support services. Your mental health matters too — PTSD and bipolar disorder need consistent care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2128-06-10 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m still taking my meds — Geodon, Seroquel, the others."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2128-06-10 09:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ve continued all your regular medications here. Your blood pressure and cholesterol meds too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2128-06-11 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re clearing you to go home today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2128-06-11 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What do I need to do when I get home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2128-06-11 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue the insulin as we adjusted — 8 in the morning, 4 at night. Eat a bland diet, take the pain pills only as needed, and don’t drive on them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2128-06-11 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if my sugar drops?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2128-06-11 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If it’s below 60, drink juice or take sugar tablets and go to the ER. If it’s consistently over 250, call your diabetes doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2128-06-11 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if the pain gets worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2128-06-11 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If it’s severe, or you can’t eat or drink, or you get a fever over 101, come back to the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2128-06-11 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I have the pain pills — how many can I take?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2128-06-11 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Up to one every four hours as needed, but no more than that. You have 40 tablets — that’s for about 10 days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2128-06-11 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2128-06-11 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You need to see your primary doctor in the next two weeks for refills. And don’t forget — back in eight weeks for stent removal with Dr. ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2128-06-11 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thanks for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2128-06-11 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2128-06-11 08:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2128-06-09 13:01:00",
    "admission_end": "2128-06-11 10:15:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 50-year-old male with chronic pancreatitis, type 1 diabetes, bipolar disorder, and PTSD was admitted for a scheduled ERCP to remove a pancreatic stent. During the procedure, a stricture in the pancreatic duct and multiple stones were found. The stricture was dilated with a balloon, stones were removed, and a new stent was placed. The patient experienced post-procedural abdominal pain and a history of hypoglycemic episodes, which were managed with adjusted insulin dosing and pain control. He was monitored for stability, advanced to a full diet, and discharged home in stable condition with instructions to follow up with his primary care provider and return in eight weeks for stent removal.",
    "problems": [
      "Chronic pancreatitis",
      "Pancreatic duct stones",
      "Pancreatic duct stricture",
      "Type 1 diabetes mellitus",
      "Hypoglycemia",
      "Abdominal pain",
      "Bipolar disorder",
      "Posttraumatic stress disorder",
      "Hypertension",
      "Hyperlipidemia"
    ]
  }
}
